<section><div class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker">The Physics</p><h2>Why earth-sheltered saunas hold heat better</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div>
  <p class="lead">A barrel sauna fights the weather; a cabin sauna leaks heat through every wall. A cave sauna is wrapped in earth — the best insulator there is. It heats faster, holds temperature longer, uses less wood or power, and the domed vault rolls steam around the room instead of trapping it at the ceiling.</p>
</div></section>

